; blast-geometry.eval — the same detonation in four geometries.
;
; A propagating blast is the kind of rule that reads correctly in a comment and
; is wrong in a corridor. `fireburst` was tuned against a THROWAWAY harness over
; pure geometry (docs/damage-system.md "Tuning a blast"); this measures the same
; thing in the REAL world, with real monsters taking real damage through the
; whole effects pipeline — resists, soak, on-hit procs and all.
;
; The monsters ARE the instrument. Each is a fixed-hp probe parked on a known
; cell, so the hp left after the blast reads off the falloff and the convergence
; directly. skel_swarm has 6 hp and dies to almost anything, so these use
; skel_warrior (22 hp) to leave headroom for a reading.
;
; spells.cat records what the tuning expected, and this is the check on it:
;   open room        5 at the centre, 3.5 around, 7 squares
;   dead end at feet 17.5 each
;   T-junction       30 at the junction  <- the worst number in the game
;
; The party is teleported OUT of each blast: a blast has no side and would catch
; them, and their deaths are not what is being measured here.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 5

; FREEZE. The instruments must hold still: the first run of this suite had two
; of its nine warriors walk out of the squares being measured and then maul the
; party, so the table described where they ended up rather than what the blast
; did to where they were. Frozen monsters still burn, still take the blast and
; still die — they simply do not act.
freeze on

; --- 1. HIS CASE: one in the middle, eight around it ----------------------
; Centre 14,12. The ring is 13..15 x 11..13; the centre cell holds the ninth.
arena open 9 9
tp 10 16
spawn skel_warrior 13 11 south
spawn skel_warrior 14 11 south
spawn skel_warrior 15 11 south
spawn skel_warrior 13 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 13 13 south
spawn skel_warrior 14 13 south
spawn skel_warrior 15 13 south
tally reset
echo === open 9x9: 3x3 surround, before ===
monsters
blast fireburst 14 12
step 5
echo === open 9x9: 3x3 surround, after ===
monsters
tally

; --- 2. a corridor: the front reflects off both ends ----------------------
arena corridor 11
tp 9 12
spawn skel_warrior 12 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 13 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 16 12 south
tally reset
echo === corridor 11: before ===
monsters
blast fireburst 14 12
step 5
echo === corridor 11: after ===
monsters
tally

; --- 3. a dead end: it reflects back onto the detonation ------------------
; The arena reports its centre AS the closed end, so 14,12 has rock behind it.
arena deadend 7
tp 20 12
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 16 12 south
tally reset
echo === dead end 7: before ===
monsters
blast fireburst 14 12
step 5
echo === dead end 7: after ===
monsters
tally

; --- 4. the T-junction: arms converge and MULTIPLY ------------------------
; The junction cell is 14,12 — the square the tuning says is the ceiling.
arena tjunction 9 5
tp 10 12
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 13 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 14 13 south
tally reset
echo === t-junction: before ===
monsters
blast fireburst 14 12
step 5
echo === t-junction: after ===
monsters
tally
state
